+# 🌉 Bridge Work Order — [P2] Redis rotation rule bug: cooldown applied to a non-exhausted slot (secondary: 2/500,000 commands, locked until Nov 1) (bridge-20261027-redis-rotation-rule)
+
+## Problem
+Refines #1322 (which correctly flagged primary quota exhaustion 500,002/500,000). Verified live 2026-10-25 via `redis_stats` + `redis_rotation_status` — the **rotation rule itself is buggy**:
+
+| Slot | Usage | Limit | Cooldown until | Active |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| primary | 500,002 | 500,000 | 2026-11-01 | no |
+| **secondary** | **2** | 500,000 | **2026-11-01** | no |
+| tertiary | 4,827 | 500,000 | — | **yes** |
+| quaternary | 1,271 | 500,000 | — | no |
+| quinary | 1,271 | 500,000 | — | no |
+| tcp-fallback | 0 | 500,000 | — | no |
+
+Secondary has consumed **0.0004 %** of its quota yet is locked for the entire month — it was almost certainly cooldown-stamped by proximity (or shared state) when primary tripped its threshold, not by its own usage. If tertiary+quaternary+quinary all exhaust before Nov 1, the chain lands on the **tcp-fallback slot with 0 usage in this window — an untested path**.
+
+## Impact (AIQ mapping)
+- AIQ-081: fallback chain has a wasted slot and an untested final fallback
+- AIQ-092: budget controls work but rotation wastes 20 % of capacity on a rule bug
+
+## Fix (smallest safe change)
+1. Change the cooldown rule: stamp cooldown ONLY on the slot whose own usage crossed soft/hard threshold; add an assertion `cooldown ⇒ usage ≥ softThreshold`
+2. Reset secondary's cooldown now (state surgery via `action_redis_flush`-adjacent admin path or manual Upstash console)
+3. Add a rotation drill to CI (weekly): force-threshold the active slot in a sandbox and assert the next slot is the least-used non-cooling one
+4. Exercise tcp-fallback once with a canary write/read and record latency in the sweep evidence
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+- [ ] `redis_rotation_status` shows secondary `cooldownUntil: null` and it receives traffic next rotation
+- [ ] Rotation drill test green in CI for 2 consecutive weeks
+- [ ] tcp-fallback evidence recorded (one successful canary op)
+- [ ] Invariant test: no slot enters cooldown below soft threshold
+
+## Reflection Evidence (why + alternatives_rejected)
+**Why:** free-tier capacity is the system's scarcest resource; a rule bug that idles 20 % of it converts into user-visible outages exactly when the other slots burn out.
+**Alternatives rejected:** (a) buying paid Upstash now — right call eventually, but the rule must be correct regardless; (b) manual rebalancing only — rots, and the drill is cheap.
+
+## Labels
+`bridge:queued` `P2-medium` `area:infra` `AIQ:081` `AIQ:092` `refines:#1322`
